# rows_rules.dat, the discretisation rules of the LPT rows and where they apply (read by lpt_tables.py).
# Generated by tools/pt_autogen (python -m pt_autogen regenerate), pt_autogen 1.2 (2026-10-17): + the derived LPT chain.
# Records:
#   rule    name | applies to | runtime action   (the rules of tools/pt_autogen/lpt_model.py RULES)
#   uses    rule row ...                         (the rows whose recipes use a rule that applies to some rows only)
#   attach  component term rule                  (every k-independent MQ0 term of the final integrand, derived)
#   kspace  row component factor interpolated k0_const
#           (the final integral adds factor x row to the weight of the component, interpolating the row in ln k at
#           the true k when interpolated is yes and reading it at k_min otherwise, and skips the k0_const rows when
#           subtract_k0_const is set)
# Order: the rules in declaration order, the attachments in component order, the k-space rows in row order.
# Counts: 12 rules, 8 attachments, 5 k-space rows.
# columns: record ...
rule    end_weights       | every FFTlog input whose support ends at an interior node | trapezoid end weight 1/2 (fftlog.trapezoid_weights) on the stage A input (core), the stage B integrands (cut at q_max), the 22 sources [k_min, 2 k_max], the 13 sources [k_min, k_max] and the final q integrand
rule    zero_pad          | the stage A input | pad_mode 'zero-pad', so P is the band-limited model and Q_n, R_n are its full integrals
rule    grid_moment       | the recipe kind M | M_n[S] = sum over the grid of dln k k^{n+3} S / (2 pi^2), the grid moment of the padded, end-weighted source or input
rule    low_ringing_phase | every transform | each (l, bias) uses its own low-ringing phase, stage A and C outputs are resampled to the common q grid, the 13 inputs stay on their own grids (conjugate to the k grid)
rule    bias_n0           | the recipe kind H with n >= 0 | kernel bias nu_n0 = 1.5 (the periodic image of the q -> 0 plateau)
rule    raise_n           | the preference raise_n_by_recurrence | the n = -2 and -3 transforms are replaced by n = -1 and -2 pairs
rule    outside_core      | a k-independent MQ0 term that is a q-space product with q^2 F = G' (G(0) = G(inf) = 0) | the k-space row -4 pi int_core dq q^2 F (the end-weighted core sum), the missing inner ball q < q_min
rule    m0_residual       | a k-independent MQ0 term that is a q-space product with a non-zero full-q integral | the k-space row H_0[F](k) - C_q, C_q the end-weighted sum of the same samples of F on the padded grid
rule    m0_constant       | the same term as m0_residual | the k-space constant of F by Parseval, the k-space grid moment of the padded, end-weighted P^2, added undamped
rule    inner_ball        | a k-independent MQ0 term given by an n >= 0 stage C transform whose source is c times that of a row R of l = 1 and n - 1 | the k-space constant 4 pi c q_min^2 R(q_min), from (q^2 R)' = c q^2 F
rule    q_max_subtraction | a k-independent constant of the MQ0 integrand | the final integral subtracts the value of the l = 0 integrand at q_max (the constant transforms to delta_D(k))
rule    linear_part       | a term first order in one tree row (a linear kind of components.dat) | the final integral subtracts it weighted by D = exp(-K^2 (X_lt + Y_lt)(q_max) / 2) and adds back D x Kaiser x P_lin(k) (lpt.LPT._linear_rows)
uses    grid_moment       X_LIN X_LIN_LT X_LIN_GT X22 X13 X10
uses    bias_n0           THETA
uses    raise_n           Y_LIN Y_LIN_LT V1 V3 T
attach  ZA     1            q_max_subtraction
attach  XI     XI_LIN       linear_part
attach  XI_XI  XI_LIN^2/2   m0_residual
attach  XI_XI  XI_LIN^2/2   m0_constant
attach  CHI    CHI          outside_core
attach  ZETA   ZETA         outside_core
attach  THETA  2*THETA      inner_ball
attach  CTR    1            q_max_subtraction
kspace  CHI_OUTSIDE   CHI    1   yes no
kspace  ZETA_OUTSIDE  ZETA   1   yes no
kspace  B2SQ_RESIDUAL XI_XI  1   yes no
kspace  B2SQ_CONST    XI_XI  1   no  yes
kspace  THETA_BALL    THETA  2   no  no
